# {{AGENT_NAME}} — Trello Project Agent (operations)

Watches Trello board `{{TRELLO_BOARD_ID}}` and reacts to card activity.
Event-driven — no cron, no servers to maintain. Installed by
[ai-automations](https://github.com/makasanaakshay/ai-automation-master);
re-run its installer to update (answers saved in `automation.config.json`).

```
Trello webhook (HEAD-probe answered; HMAC-SHA1 verified when TRELLO_API_SECRET set)
  → Cloudflare Worker relay            scripts/trello-agent/relay/worker.js
  → repository_dispatch                .github/workflows/trello-agent.yml
  → agent-run.sh                       restore state → resolve → playbook → save state
```

| Trigger | Playbook | Output (one Trello comment) |
|---|---|---|
| Card enters **{{LIST_ANALYZE_NAME}}** | `analyze` | Options + trade-offs + recommendation, or numbered questions |
| Human comment on a {{LIST_ANALYZE_NAME}} card | `respond` | Answer / updated proposal / remaining questions |
| Card enters **{{LIST_IMPLEMENT_NAME}}** (or comment there) | `implement` | PR into `{{PR_BASE}}` — or questions if unclear |

State lives on the orphan branch `trello-agent-state` (`state/<card_id>.json`:
list_id, phase, last_comment_date, branch, pr_url). Every run re-fetches truth
from the Trello API and diffs against it — webhook payloads are only
doorbells. Agent comments are prefixed `{{AGENT_MARKER}} — `; the resolver and
relay both skip marker comments (loop protection). Comment recency is tracked
by action `date`.

## Operating

- **Recover / backfill:** Actions → *Trello Project Agent* → *Run workflow* — empty `item_id` reconciles both watched lists + tracked cards; a card id processes one.
- **Transcripts:** every run uploads `.agent-out/` as an artifact.
- **Model:** `AI_MODEL` in `scripts/trello-agent/env.sh` (currently `{{AI_MODEL}}`, brain `{{BRAIN_NAME}}`).
- **Pause:** `api.sh PUT "/1/webhooks/<webhook_id>?active=false"` (list them: `api.sh GET "/1/tokens/<token>/webhooks"`).
- **Known blind spot:** moving a card back into a watched list silently — re-trigger with a comment or a manual run.

## Local dry-run (safe — needs TRELLO_KEY + TRELLO_TOKEN exported)

```bash
DRY_RUN=1 bash scripts/trello-agent/agent-run.sh                 # reconcile scan
DRY_RUN=1 ITEM_ID=<card_id> bash scripts/trello-agent/agent-run.sh
```

## Guardrails

- Trello writes are **comments only** — the agent never moves, archives, or edits cards; humans own the board.
- PRs are **always against `{{PR_BASE}}`** (branch `{{BRANCH_PREFIX}}/<kebab-slug>`); the agent never merges and never pushes to `{{PR_BASE}}` directly.
- `--dangerously-skip-permissions` only inside the disposable CI runner; local runs are `DRY_RUN` and stop before any AI call.
